{
  "comment": "The vectors binding cyfr-spawn (apps/spawn, Go) and its clients, the MCP bridge (apps/mcp-bridge/spawn-client.mjs, Node) and the builder (apps/locus/lib/locus/spawner.ex, Elixir): the spawner accepts every valid request and refuses every invalid one with its code, every side encodes each frame to the bytes given, and the clients understand every reply. `frames` are the stdio and attach streams every client carries; `control_frames` are the control stream (4) of a spawn that asked for a control channel with `control: true`, carrying Cyfr.RunnerControl lines (tests/fixtures/runner_control.json) verbatim between a worker service and its runner's fd 3, and a zero-length one ending the stream. A client that never asks for the channel refuses a control frame. A spawn of any pool may carry `memory_bytes`, its memory bound, from 16777216 to 1099511627776: zero is not 'no bound', and a bound that is not a whole number of bytes in that range is refused. Every `exited` says whether the kernel killed processes of the spawn at that bound (`memory_exceeded`), and a spawner that cannot enforce a bound refuses the spawn as `memory_unavailable`.",
